      "## What a diagnostic is—and is not",
      "A diagnostic is a **starting measurement** used to guide preparation. It is not a prediction made with certainty, and it is not a substitute for the official examination.",
      "A low baseline can be useful because it identifies where learning should begin. A high baseline can also be misleading if it was produced by repeated questions, open-book assistance, unusually easy items, or a sample concentrated in the learner's strongest subjects.",
