      "- Do not use notes, search engines, or answer explanations.\n- Work in one planned sitting when possible.\n- Use a pace appropriate to the selected exam version.\n- Record interruptions rather than silently treating an interrupted attempt as comparable to a controlled one.\n- Use questions the learner has not previously seen whenever possible.",
