    "whyItMatters": "The NCE requires retrieval across a broad body of material. A concept understood once may not be available several weeks later. Repeated rereading can make a page feel familiar without demonstrating that the learner can produce or apply its meaning independently. Research on learning and memory supports two useful principles: - **Retrieval practice:** attempting to recall information can strengthen later retention more effectively than spending the same time only restudying it.\n- **Distributed practice:** revisiting material over separated sessions generally supports longer retention better than concentrating all exposure into one period. Corrective feedback matters, particularly after multiple-choice practice, because it helps repair errors and reduces the risk of retaining distractor information.",
